{{!
    @template tool_vae/roles_install_page

    The page of the VAE roles, below its heading, when no role is asked for: what the page does, then each group of
    presets (the base ones, the optional ones) under its heading, with its warning and its table.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\roles_install_page. The template holds no logic.
    Every text is escaped (double braces), except two keys of HTML (triple braces): headinghtml, a heading of the core
    ($output->heading()); tablehtml, the table drawn by the template tool_vae/table.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * intro - string, what the page does
    * groups - array of groups, each with:
        * headinghtml - HTML, the heading of the group
        * warning - false, or a string: the warning of the optional roles
        * tablehtml - HTML, the table of the presets of the group

    Example context (json):
    {
        "intro": "Creates the roles of the plugin from the presets shipped with it. Nothing is created by opening this page.",
        "groups": [
            {
                "headinghtml": "<h3>The three base roles</h3>",
                "warning": false,
                "tablehtml": "<table class=\"generaltable tool-vae-roles\"><tbody><tr><td>Vaeiste</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            },
            {
                "headinghtml": "<h3>Two optional roles</h3>",
                "warning": "These roles add the right to write a positioning of the structure.",
                "tablehtml": "<table class=\"generaltable tool-vae-roles\"><tbody><tr><td>VAE manager</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
        ]
    }
}}
<p>{{intro}}</p>
{{#groups}}
{{{headinghtml}}}
{{#warning}}
<p class="text-muted small">{{warning}}</p>
{{/warning}}
{{{tablehtml}}}
{{/groups}}
